SUMMARY:Soul Sessions: The Human Rights
DESCRIPTION:The Human Rights first came together in 2007\, around the talents and vision of lead singer and Toronto Reggae lion Friendlyness (Big Sugar\, Culture Shock\, Truth And Rights)\, drummer Eric Woolston (Maylee Todd\, The Hooded Fang)\, versatile bassman Tyler Wagler and the band’s original keyboardist Bernie Pitters (Toots & The Maytals\, Hit Squad)\, who passed away in 2023 and in whose loving memory the band continues forward. \nEase into the weekend with Soul Sessions every Friday night at Union Summer. From smooth R&B and classic Motown to timeless hits across the decades\, our live performers reimagine the songs you love with fresh energy and irresistible groove. It’s a feel-good night of music\, movement\, and nostalgia—guaranteed to get you dancing under the open sky.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/soul-sessions-union-summer-2/
