SUMMARY:Indigenous Spotlight Series: Mâmawin’towin
DESCRIPTION:Our Indigenous Spotlight Series highlights top contemporary Indigenous music artists on the scene. \nMeriläinen Müsic Inc.\, founded by Marc and Laura Meriläinen\, is a majority Indigenous owned full-service record label providing professional music industry services to emerging and established artists. Meriläinen Müsic Inc. is committed to advancing and promoting the careers and opportunities within the music industry for all artists while also specializing in serving the Indigenous Artist community. \nCo-led by celebrated Métis fiddler Alyssa Katrine and JUNO-nominated and CFMA Award–winning Métis singer-songwriter Amanda Rheaume\, Mâmawin’towin brings together an exceptional acoustic ensemble rooted in Métis musical tradition. The group has toured internationally\, most recently performing at World Expo 2025 in Osaka\, Japan\, as well as in Australia\, sharing Métis music with global audiences. Joined by acclaimed multi-instrumentalists Danton Delbaere-Sawchuk and Kyler Tapscott\, the ensemble blends driving Métis fiddle tunes\, rich vocal harmonies\, and powerful storytelling inspired by Métis history and community. Drawing on the warmth and spirit of a Métis kitchen party\, their performances celebrate resilience\, kinship\, and the enduring vitality of Métis music.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/contemporary-indigenous-mamawintowin/
LOCATION:Union\, 65 Front Street West\, Toronto\, ON\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Union Summer
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://torontounion.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/July-6-2026-Mamawintowin-Photo-.png
GEO:43.6453166;-79.3804073
