SUMMARY:Monday Blues: Glenn Marais and the Mojo Train
DESCRIPTION:Ease into your week with Monday Blues at Union Summer\, featuring two shows of blues music showcasing a range of artists. \nGlenn Marais and The Mojo Train are a blues-rock band known for high-energy live performances\, tight arrangements\, and improvisational musicianship. Their sound is driven by deep grooves\, expressive guitar work\, and soulful storytelling\, creating an engaging and dynamic live experience. \nLed by Glenn Marais on guitar\, harmonica\, and vocals\, the band also features Manny DeGrandis on bass\, Jeff Saulnier on drums\, and Jesse Karwat on keyboards\, each contributing to a full\, layered live sound rooted in blues and rock traditions. \nThe Toronto Blues Society (TBS) is a non-profit organization dedicated to promoting and preserving the legacy of blues music. As it celebrates over 40 years of supporting the genre\, it continues to honour its roots while fostering future generations of artists. \nThis program is in partnership with the Toronto Blues Society (TBS).
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/monday-blues-glenn-marais-and-the-mojo-train/
