SUMMARY:Spotlight on Women: Phoenix Pagliacci
DESCRIPTION:Explore a lineup of women in music with a roster of Toronto’s top female talent. \npHoenix Pagliacci is a Toronto-based R&B and Hip-Hop artist\, producer\, songwriter\, and advocate. Inspired by a lifelong passion for music\, she began singing and playing piano at a young age and has since built a reputation for her versatility as both a vocalist and rapper. \nAs a founding member of The Sorority and one half of the R&B duo TRP.P\, pHoenix has developed a distinctive artistic voice while continuing to expand her creative practice through music production. A participant in the Women in the Studio program\, she is committed to pushing boundaries and creating opportunities for the next generation of artists. \nThrough her company\, Pagliacci Studios\, she provides a supportive space where young women can learn\, collaborate\, and grow creatively. \nThis program is in partnership with City Hall Live\, a City of Toronto program that creates paid opportunities for local bands and provides accessible live music experiences for residents and visitors.
URL:https://torontounion.ca/event/spotlight-on-women-phoenix-pagliacci/
